loop 14 | Tool=Write, Args={"file_path":"/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp_server/1083718880_biocontext-ai_skill-to-mcp/skills/single-cell-rna-qc/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: single-cell-rna-qc\ndescription: Performs quality control on single-cell RNA-seq data using standard metrics and filtering thresholds\n---\n\n# Single-Cell RNA-seq Quality Control\n\nThis skill provides guidance on performing quality control (QC) for single-cell RNA sequencing data.\n\n## When to use this skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Processing raw single-cell RNA-seq data\n- Evaluating cell quality before downstream analysis\n- Identifying low-quality cells or doublets\n\n## QC Metrics\n\n### Key Metrics to Evaluate\n\n1. **Library size** - Total counts per cell\n2. **Number of detected genes** - Genes with non-zero expression\n3. **Mitochondrial percentage** - Indicator of cell stress/death\n4. **Ribosomal percentage** - Can indicate technical issues\n\n### Typical Thresholds\n\n- Min library size: 500-1000 counts\n- Min genes: 200-500\n- Max mitochondrial: 10-20%\n\n## Example Code\n\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\n\n# Load data\nadata = sc.read_h5ad(\"raw_data.h5ad\")\n\n# Calculate QC metrics\nadata.obs['n_counts'] = adata.X.sum(axis=1)\nadata.obs['n_genes'] = (adata.X > 0).sum(axis=1)\n\n# Filter cells\nhigh_quality = (\n    (adata.obs['n_counts'] > 1000) &\n    (adata.obs['n_genes'] > 500)\n)\nadata = adata[high_quality]\n```\n\n## References\n\n- Luecken & Theis, Molecular Systems Biology (2019)\n- Scverse tutorials: https://scverse.org\n"}
